WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.522 --> 00:00:01.625
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.625 --> 00:00:04.963
Today's message is find your gift.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:06.884
Over to you, Cicely Tyson.

00:00:06.884 --> 00:00:08.930
(rooster crows)

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.723
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.723 --> 00:00:14.414
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:17.914
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.922 --> 00:00:20.639
- There was a time when I had

00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:22.905
two or three jobs in the same day.

00:00:22.905 --> 00:00:24.070
I'd go here and do a little bit,

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:26.510
here and do a little bit,
here and do a little bit,

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:30.465
and people began to talk
about this new actress,

00:00:30.465 --> 00:00:31.548
Cicely Tyson.

00:00:32.423 --> 00:00:34.756
And next thing I knew I was,

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.464
here in front of you.

00:00:37.464 --> 00:00:39.547
(laughs)

00:00:40.949 --> 00:00:44.232
My mother wasn't happy
about what I was doing.

00:00:44.232 --> 00:00:46.039
She didn't like it.

00:00:46.039 --> 00:00:49.390
She told me I couldn't stay
in her house and do that,

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.890
whatever that was.

00:00:53.325 --> 00:00:56.515
I was called by Vinnit Caroll

00:00:56.515 --> 00:00:59.265
and asked to come and read a play

00:01:00.273 --> 00:01:02.389
called Dark of the Moon.

00:01:02.389 --> 00:01:06.363
And it was to be done at the Y in Harlem.

00:01:06.363 --> 00:01:09.909
My mother heard that I
was going to do this play.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:11.654
She told my sister,

00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:15.821
"Hmm, she's going up there
and make a fool of herself."

00:01:16.721 --> 00:01:18.158
Okay.

00:01:18.158 --> 00:01:21.214
So I decided to invite her.

00:01:21.214 --> 00:01:25.006
And she came and she brought a friend.

00:01:25.006 --> 00:01:28.029
I made sure I knew exactly
where she was going to sit

00:01:28.029 --> 00:01:32.146
so that I wouldn't look
in that direction, okay.

00:01:32.146 --> 00:01:34.123
From the moment I walked out on the stage,

00:01:34.123 --> 00:01:36.540
I heard her say, "Oh my god."

00:01:40.214 --> 00:01:43.603
She kept talking to her
friend all during the time.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.151
She thought she was whispering.

00:01:46.151 --> 00:01:48.264
But I could hear every word she said.

00:01:48.264 --> 00:01:49.764
It drove me crazy.

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:52.606
At the end of this play

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:58.591
I come out and my mother
is standing at the door,

00:01:58.591 --> 00:02:02.945
accepting congratulatory
remarks from the people.

00:02:02.945 --> 00:02:04.512
(laughs)

00:02:04.512 --> 00:02:07.822
"Yes I always knew, ever
since she was a little girl,

00:02:07.822 --> 00:02:11.457
that she was going, you know
she like to sing and dance.

00:02:11.457 --> 00:02:15.124
And so I always knew she
was going to do this."

00:02:16.848 --> 00:02:19.133
I said, "Wait a minute."

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.709
My mother who put me out of her house

00:02:21.709 --> 00:02:24.413
and didn't speak to me
for almost three years,

00:02:24.413 --> 00:02:28.164
is standing there telling
this bare-faced story

00:02:28.164 --> 00:02:29.160
to these people.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:29.993
Right?

00:02:31.598 --> 00:02:34.515
And so I knew that it was something

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:37.292
within me

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:39.941
that she felt

00:02:41.631 --> 00:02:43.209
was a gift.

00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:44.639
- So I'd like to say that Michael Jordan

00:02:44.639 --> 00:02:47.307
is not the greatest
basketball player of all time.

00:02:47.307 --> 00:02:48.927
The greatest basketball player of all time

00:02:48.927 --> 00:02:50.959
is a manager at Starbucks.

00:02:50.959 --> 00:02:53.397
Because he never laced up.

00:02:53.397 --> 00:02:56.688
Because he never realized
that that was his real gift.

00:02:56.688 --> 00:02:58.165
And I think that so many people

00:02:58.165 --> 00:03:01.006
walk through life that way.

00:03:01.006 --> 00:03:03.445
I think so many people have
not discovered their gift.

00:03:03.445 --> 00:03:05.720
Maybe not you guys as
part of Believe Nation.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:07.559
But I think most of the world

00:03:07.559 --> 00:03:09.283
has not discovered their gift.

00:03:09.283 --> 00:03:11.247
And they know they should
be doing something else,

00:03:11.247 --> 00:03:13.220
but instead they're doing this thing.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.825
Because it's safe,
because it's comfortable,

00:03:14.825 --> 00:03:16.611
because it's convenient,
because it pays the bills,

00:03:16.611 --> 00:03:18.324
because, because, because, because,

00:03:18.324 --> 00:03:21.474
all the practical reasons why
we do the things that we do.

00:03:21.474 --> 00:03:23.289
Instead of following our heart

00:03:23.289 --> 00:03:25.164
and doing the thing
that we should be doing.

00:03:25.164 --> 00:03:26.437
I think that's super common.

00:03:26.437 --> 00:03:31.288
I think we all have Michael
Jordan level talent at something

00:03:31.288 --> 00:03:33.497
and most people have barely
scratched the surface

00:03:33.497 --> 00:03:35.920
of understanding what's possible for them.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.275
If you don't know what it
is that you want to do,

00:03:38.275 --> 00:03:39.275
you need to explore.

00:03:39.275 --> 00:03:41.232
Say yes to things.

00:03:41.232 --> 00:03:42.296
Try things.

00:03:42.296 --> 00:03:43.550
That idea that you have,

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:45.924
just get started on it.

00:03:45.924 --> 00:03:47.890
Find some small way to build momentum

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:48.890
and get started.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:50.233
What we tend to do

00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:53.904
is we build this dream up
in some big huge thing.

00:03:53.904 --> 00:03:55.663
This big vision that we want,

00:03:55.663 --> 00:03:57.695
which is amazing, I love the thinking big.

00:03:57.695 --> 00:03:59.164
But then because it's so big,

00:03:59.164 --> 00:04:01.060
we don't take any action on it.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:03.306
We tell ourselves that we can't do that

00:04:03.306 --> 00:04:04.773
until we have funding,

00:04:04.773 --> 00:04:07.734
or can't do that until I meet this person

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:08.749
or I get this connection

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:10.729
or I move to that country, right?

00:04:10.729 --> 00:04:13.963
We build up all of these things
that have to happen first

00:04:13.963 --> 00:04:17.004
before we do anything to go
an accomplish that big goal.

00:04:17.004 --> 00:04:18.502
And guess what happens?

00:04:18.502 --> 00:04:19.722
Nothing.

00:04:19.722 --> 00:04:23.024
You just sit on that idea
for the rest of your life.

00:04:23.024 --> 00:04:25.835
And you die with your
song still left inside you

00:04:25.835 --> 00:04:28.309
instead of releasing it to the world.

00:04:28.309 --> 00:04:29.713
I love the big thinking.

00:04:29.713 --> 00:04:31.801
I love the big vision and the dreaming.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.010
It's important.

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.391
It's motivating, it
drives us, it's inspiring.

00:04:35.391 --> 00:04:39.454
But at the same time you have
to take action immediately.

00:04:39.454 --> 00:04:42.465
As soon as you set some
big huge goal for yourself,

00:04:42.465 --> 00:04:45.718
that day you need to start building

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.424
some kind of momentum to it.

00:04:47.424 --> 00:04:50.060
If your big goal is to write a book,

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:51.795
and have it be a best seller,

00:04:51.795 --> 00:04:53.628
and get it published
through a major publisher,

00:04:53.628 --> 00:04:54.645
that's what it is,

00:04:54.645 --> 00:04:57.304
you got a book inside you
and it has to come out.

00:04:57.304 --> 00:04:59.707
Start, start writing the book.

00:04:59.707 --> 00:05:03.394
Start researching authors
and how they had success.

00:05:03.394 --> 00:05:05.315
Start going to industry events

00:05:05.315 --> 00:05:07.234
and getting to know what
the process is all about.

00:05:07.234 --> 00:05:09.592
Start trying to line up
coffee meetings or interviews

00:05:09.592 --> 00:05:11.931
with people who've had
some success along the way.

00:05:11.931 --> 00:05:14.100
Look for meet up groups in your local area

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.476
to stat building some kind of momentum.

00:05:15.476 --> 00:05:16.929
Something, take action.

00:05:16.929 --> 00:05:18.496
You want to be a YouTuber.

00:05:18.496 --> 00:05:20.062
Great, start.

00:05:20.062 --> 00:05:21.519
Build a channel, make your first video.

00:05:21.519 --> 00:05:22.620
It's going to suck.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:23.682
That's okay.

00:05:23.682 --> 00:05:25.483
Do it again, and do it
again, and do it again.

00:05:25.483 --> 00:05:27.803
Whatever that big dream of yours is,

00:05:27.803 --> 00:05:31.731
you need to find a way to
get started immediately

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:34.176
and build some momentum.

00:05:34.176 --> 00:05:36.325
And if you don't know it, then you explore

00:05:36.325 --> 00:05:39.027
until you find the thing
that makes you come alive.

00:05:39.027 --> 00:05:41.931
And at the beginning,
this really important,

00:05:41.931 --> 00:05:43.348
at the beginning,

00:05:45.197 --> 00:05:46.447
it's from here.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:49.166
The thing that you want to do

00:05:49.166 --> 00:05:51.188
is not going to make
any sense practically.

00:05:51.188 --> 00:05:54.201
You're going to come up with all
of these practical reasons why

00:05:54.201 --> 00:05:56.777
you should not go out and do that.

00:05:56.777 --> 00:05:58.450
And so you're going to
stay on this straight path

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.188
that you've been on before.

00:06:00.188 --> 00:06:02.021
But how happy are you?

00:06:03.643 --> 00:06:06.072
And imagine fifty more years
of doing this same thing

00:06:06.072 --> 00:06:08.239
that you don't like doing.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:10.287
And it doesn't mean that you just

00:06:10.287 --> 00:06:13.744
throw everything away and
go all the way out here.

00:06:13.744 --> 00:06:16.045
You don't have to burn
the boats necessarily.

00:06:16.045 --> 00:06:17.779
I'm not that kind of person.

00:06:17.779 --> 00:06:20.196
But you have to do something.

00:06:21.753 --> 00:06:23.290
You have to take a little bit of time

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.654
away from this straight path

00:06:24.654 --> 00:06:26.549
to play out here.

00:06:26.549 --> 00:06:28.325
Because if you don't,

00:06:28.325 --> 00:06:29.884
you're never going to
do anything out here,

00:06:29.884 --> 00:06:31.356
you're never going to get there.

00:06:31.356 --> 00:06:34.375
Daily consistent action of some kind

00:06:34.375 --> 00:06:36.521
towards the attainment of your dreams.

00:06:36.521 --> 00:06:38.601
It's important.

00:06:38.601 --> 00:06:40.979
Everybody has a dream.

00:06:40.979 --> 00:06:43.969
Everybody has some big
thing that they want to do.

00:06:43.969 --> 00:06:47.564
And 99% of people just
complain why they can't do it.

00:06:47.564 --> 00:06:49.646
Don't be that person.

00:06:49.646 --> 00:06:51.924
You already have the
resourcefulness inside you

00:06:51.924 --> 00:06:53.725
to move forward on your dreams.

00:06:53.725 --> 00:06:55.110
Now what are you going to do about it?

00:06:55.110 --> 00:06:57.928
Take action or complain?

00:06:57.928 --> 00:06:59.532
Get to it.

00:06:59.532 --> 00:07:00.788
So the question of the day today is,

00:07:00.788 --> 00:07:02.868
I'm curious, what is that
story you're telling yourself

00:07:02.868 --> 00:07:04.284
as to why you're not going out

00:07:04.284 --> 00:07:05.865
and accomplishing your bigger goal.

00:07:05.865 --> 00:07:06.862
What are you telling yourself?

00:07:06.862 --> 00:07:07.862
What's the reason?

00:07:07.862 --> 00:07:09.462
What's the excuse, what's the complaint?

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:12.806
Put it down and then laugh at it.

00:07:12.806 --> 00:07:14.735
And understand that
you're better than this

00:07:14.735 --> 00:07:16.909
and remember who you are.

00:07:16.909 --> 00:07:18.931
Leave in the comments,
I'm curious to find out.

00:07:18.931 --> 00:07:20.954
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Calvin Simpson,

00:07:20.954 --> 00:07:23.162
Calvin, thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book

00:07:23.162 --> 00:07:24.362
Your One Word.

00:07:24.362 --> 00:07:25.570
Really means a lot to me

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.595
and I hope you are enjoying the read.

00:07:27.595 --> 00:07:29.000
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:30.058
I believe in you.

00:07:30.058 --> 00:07:31.864
Hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:07:31.864 --> 00:07:33.940
and whatever your one word is.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.539
Much love and I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:07:36.539 --> 00:07:38.956
for another shot of espresso.

00:07:39.819 --> 00:07:41.645
♫ I wake up every morning

00:07:41.645 --> 00:07:45.062
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:07:48.652 --> 00:07:51.771
- I just really worked on my gift.

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:55.140
I realized that all of
us are born with a gift,

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:56.717
but you got to hone it.

00:07:56.717 --> 00:07:59.635
You're not going to become great,

00:07:59.635 --> 00:08:01.468
and we talk about the school of greatness,

00:08:01.468 --> 00:08:02.727
you know we talk about,

00:08:02.727 --> 00:08:05.268
you know, greatness is upon you.

00:08:05.268 --> 00:08:08.631
And I realized that my gift
wasn't going to create itself.

00:08:08.631 --> 00:08:10.721
My gift wasn't going to nurture itself.

00:08:10.721 --> 00:08:13.139
My gift wasn't going to perfect itself.

00:08:13.139 --> 00:08:14.902
That was something I had to do.

00:08:14.902 --> 00:08:16.855
And so, man before you know it,

00:08:16.855 --> 00:08:18.172
we did a video that went viral.

00:08:18.172 --> 00:08:19.949
I think it's got over 50 million hits now.

00:08:19.949 --> 00:08:23.068
And we turned our passion into our profit.

00:08:23.068 --> 00:08:24.734
- I love it man, I love it.

00:08:24.734 --> 00:08:26.870
- Your gift can be anything.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:28.937
You can't look at it as
simply running, jumping,

00:08:28.937 --> 00:08:30.419
singing and dancing.

00:08:30.419 --> 00:08:31.483
But I tell you one thing,

00:08:31.483 --> 00:08:34.850
your gift is the thing that
you do the absolute best

00:08:34.850 --> 00:08:37.003
with the least amount of effort.

00:08:37.003 --> 00:08:39.217
For me, it was comedy.

00:08:39.217 --> 00:08:41.299
So once you identify it then,

00:08:41.299 --> 00:08:43.264
that's the beginning of it.

00:08:43.264 --> 00:08:45.168
But there's a lot of work to do

00:08:45.168 --> 00:08:47.608
even after you identify your gift.

00:08:47.608 --> 00:08:50.411
You can believe you're
something or you won't,

00:08:50.411 --> 00:08:52.020
but if you don't work towards it,

00:08:52.020 --> 00:08:54.490
you just sitting there,
it's going to be empty.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.046
- Well my message to the
youth pretty much, man,

00:08:56.046 --> 00:08:58.018
is to follow your dreams,
you know what I mean.

00:08:58.018 --> 00:08:59.773
I think a lot of people get caught up

00:08:59.773 --> 00:09:01.547
and get side tracked

00:09:01.547 --> 00:09:04.678
by what's happening around
them and what's cool.

00:09:04.678 --> 00:09:06.350
People always ignore their gift,

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:08.515
not realizing that gift is
what's going to take you

00:09:08.515 --> 00:09:10.506
out of your poverty, take
you out of your situation,

00:09:10.506 --> 00:09:13.691
that gift is the ultimate element

00:09:13.691 --> 00:09:16.475
that God provided for you to
get you out of any situation

00:09:16.475 --> 00:09:18.721
or to take you to what
you're destined for.

00:09:18.721 --> 00:09:21.466
You know, some people they're
just great at certain things,

00:09:21.466 --> 00:09:25.874
but because music or
modeling or film is cool,

00:09:25.874 --> 00:09:27.577
they alienate what their gifts are

00:09:27.577 --> 00:09:29.227
just to be a part of something that is

00:09:29.227 --> 00:09:32.847
pursued to be or persuaded to be cool.

00:09:32.847 --> 00:09:34.403
So I always feel like, you know, my method

00:09:34.403 --> 00:09:36.294
and message always has been

00:09:36.294 --> 00:09:38.070
just follow the gift that you have,

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:39.790
put a lot of emphasize in it.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:42.031
Concentrate on what you
feel that you're great it,

00:09:42.031 --> 00:09:43.933
because what you're great
in is always going to be

00:09:43.933 --> 00:09:45.175
what pulls you out

00:09:45.175 --> 00:09:46.971
of the worst situations
that you could ever imagine

00:09:46.971 --> 00:09:48.947
and put you in a better
situation like we in today.

